 "refresh_note_2026_11_23": "Full weekly re-extract 2026-11-23 (Kevin-approved run of the standard WP Engine tools; extract probes identical to probes_2026-11-16, outputs written to the site-dir mcp_extract_out/ and deleted after download). Live at extract time: 1,267 published products, 1,267 courses, 8,463 published pages, 1,342 sample-meta quizzes. Rebuild: 1,267 programs; 1,255 with sample + sample URL attached (12 products have no qualifying sample set yet \u2014 several are launches parked in repair; the server reports their samples as unavailable, nothing invented); 1,203 with practice count; 131 with facts; 40 with weights; 87 quizzes excluded by the sampling fence, all as not-a-fixed-size-sample-set (free full practice exams etc.). Sampling fence UNCHANGED (FIXED_SAMPLE_SIZE=20, fixed set only, recorded form must match size). One parser robustness fix in build_data.py parse_page: prose commas before 'practice questions' (e.g. 'the curriculum, practice questions, and mock exams') produced a digit-less capture that crashed int() on 4 pages; the count search now takes the first digit-bearing match \u2014 identical output for every page that built before. Digital SAT practice_question_count remains page-derived (program page reads 50,000); the sat record's description field carries the Kevin-approved claim (2026-11-13); build_data.py does not emit description \u2014 re-applied after this build."
